From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Glats <glats@local>
Date: 2026-07-04
Subject: [PATCH] smb: disable UseCCache during NTLMSSP anonymous fallback

gvfs unconditionally sets smbc_setOptionUseCCache(smb_context, 1) at init.
With samba 4.23+, when UseCCache=TRUE and no Kerberos credential cache
exists, smbc_stat() returns EINVAL (errno=22) instead of falling back to
NTLMSSP. This prevents anonymous/guest SMB mounting from gvfs.

Fix: disable UseCCache when enabling NTLMSSP fallback for anonymous mounts.

See: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gvfs/-/work_items/857
---
 daemon/gvfsbackendsmb.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/daemon/gvfsbackendsmb.c b/daemon/gvfsbackendsmb.c
index 48eaf6e..c6cd0b4 100644
--- a/daemon/gvfsbackendsmb.c
+++ b/daemon/gvfsbackendsmb.c
@@ -567,6 +567,9 @@ do_mount (GVfsBackend *backend,
         {
           g_debug ("do_mount - enabling NTLMSSP fallback\n");
           smbc_setOptionFallbackAfterKerberos (op_backend->smb_context, 1);
+          /* Samba 4.23+ returns EINVAL when UseCCache is set but no Kerberos
+           * credential cache exists, preventing NTLMSSP anonymous fallback. */
+          smbc_setOptionUseCCache (op_backend->smb_context, 0);
         }
 
       op_backend->mount_try ++;
